Package: panelspatialprobit
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Panel Spatial Probit and Ordered Probit Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Package", "Author", email = "nonoghislain@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian Markov chain Monte Carlo estimation of spatial probit
    and spatial ordered probit models for panel data. Supports spatial
    autoregressive, spatial Durbin, spatial lag of X, spatial error and
    combined specifications with time-invariant or time-varying weights;
    pooled, random, spatially autocorrelated and correlated random effects;
    time effects; dynamic models with lagged outcomes (Wooldridge initial
    conditions) or latent autoregressive dynamics; normal or Student-t
    errors; and
    impacts (direct, indirect and total marginal effects) on outcome
    probabilities. Sampling builds on the data augmentation approach of
    Albert and Chib (1993) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1993.10476321>, its spatial
    extension by LeSage (2000) <doi:10.1111/j.1538-4632.2000.tb00413.x> and
    the panel models of Kakamu and Wago (2005).
